			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-24T06:25:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				25
			],
			"Message": "style(Maintain): Normalize shell script whitespace conventions across build helpers\n\nNormalize indentation, pipe alignment, and redirect spacing in all Maintain/*.sh scripts by removing trailing tab indentation inside case branches, collapsing `2> /dev/null` → `2>/dev/null`, collapsing `> \"$file\"` → `>\"$file\"`, and aligning comment/continuation lines to 2-space indents. Affected scripts include Build, Run, Dev-Mountain, Format, Integration/SmokeProfiles, Profile, Release, Release/Build, Repository/*, Save, Script/CleanGenerated, Script/GenerateRouteManifest, Script/PostHogCapture, Script/ProfileMarker, Script/ResolveIdentity, Script/ResolveProductConfig, Script/SignBundle, Script/TierEnvironment, and Test/TelemetryTreeShake.\nThese changes enforce the project's shell-script maintenance conventions without altering any functional behaviour.",
			"SHA": "c0a715681a3b4a09b2202854caeefdf226489807"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T16:31:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule to enforce PascalCase and atomize state\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from c2b71ca to 27f4c37 to systematically enforce the project-wide PascalCase naming convention and decompose monolithic state structures in the Mountain native backend.\n\n**Mountain:** Refactor state management by splitting large files into atomic modules (e.g., `MapLockError`, `DispatchDeltaWorkspaceFolders`) and renaming state structs to `Struct` to align with the reverse-hierarchical import pattern (`State::Struct`). Enforce PascalCase across Tauri commands, helper functions, and DTOs, including `AirClient` and all `Vine`/`IPC` layer handlers. Split service files into single-purpose modules (e.g., `Binary::Initialize`, `ExtensionManagement::Scanner`) to reduce boilerplate.\n\n**Impact:** Callers now utilize fully qualified paths (e.g., `Binary::Main::Entry::Fn`), significantly improving code clarity, maintainability, and strict adherence to the `CLAUDE.md` architectural standards.",
			"SHA": "0c574427e1e49bed65f9bf25b1d67c92b538615f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T16:18:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule to enforce PascalCase in Mountain DNS, TLS, and IPC\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule to commit c2b71ca to systematically enforce the project-wide PascalCase naming convention across the Mountain native backend. This aligns the DNS, TLS, and IPC layers with the standards mandated in CLAUDE.md.\n\n**Mountain:** Refactor Tauri commands, helper functions, and struct fields to replace snake_case with PascalCase. New diagnostic commands (`DnsGetForwardAllowlist`, `TlsInitialize`) and internal utilities (`GetMemoryUsage`) are updated. IPC handlers for `ConfigurationBridge` and `WindAdvancedSync` now export PascalCase identifiers, with all call sites in `WindServiceHandlers`, `ProcessManagement`, and `Track::Effect` adjusted accordingly.\n\nThese changes eliminate naming inconsistencies across the native backend and IPC boundary, ensuring strict adherence to the effect-based architectural principles.",
			"SHA": "96c20f32280da1aa1744e715c9e915caaee241fe"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T16:15:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Land): Sync Element submodule to enforce PascalCase naming\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to commit dcce417 to systematically enforce the project-wide PascalCase naming convention across the native backend and UI layers.\n\n**Mountain:** Refactor IPC utilities, Tauri command handlers (Dns, Tls, Process, Health), and gRPC field mappings to replace snake_case with PascalCase. Align `effect!` macro parameter extraction and error bindings with the `Error`/`E` convention.\n\n**Output:** Update TypeScript polyfills and proxy layers to match renamed Tauri commands (e.g., `ProcessGetExecPath`, `CocoonExtensionHostHealth`) to ensure correct frontend invocation.\n\n**Wind:** Align the Vine notification stream implementation with PascalCase identifiers (`VineSubscribeNotifications`, `VineSubscriberCount`) for all Tauri interactions.\n\nThese changes eliminate style inconsistencies across the Rust/TypeScript boundary, ensuring strict adherence to the Effect-based architectural principles and the `CLAUDE.md` naming standards.",
			"SHA": "9547753ed0026e6e1d3f42191e329c4c351d3ef2"
		}
